.git
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/src/webdist
assets
deploy
*.md
*.bat
*.cmd
lib

# Dockerfile.test builds turbollm/dist on the HOST first, then COPYs it in,
# rather than bundling in-container (that OOM-crashed the 1.9 GiB test VM —
# see Dockerfile.test's header comment). Everything else stays excluded:
# node_modules is still always installed fresh in-container (a host
# node_modules would carry host-OS native bindings into a Linux image), and
# the other Dockerfiles' own multi-stage builds are unaffected since they
# never reference the host's turbollm/dist at all.
!turbollm/dist
!turbollm/dist/**
!turbollm/src/webdist
!turbollm/src/webdist/**